        "original_id": "6f2e5f86-bf65-580b-8807-5ff38ba8c162",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Iftikhar Ali Khan Pataudi, Mansoor Ali Khan Pataudi\n- Roles: Nawab of Pataudi, captain of the India cricket team\n- Organizations: India national cricket team\n- Events: 1946 tour to England, 26th Amendment to the Constitution of India\n\nFacts:\n- Iftikhar Ali Khan Pataudi was born on 16 March 1910.\n- In 1946, Iftikhar Ali Khan Pataudi captained the India national cricket team on its tour to England.\n- Iftikhar Ali Khan Pataudi was the 8th Nawab of Pataudi.\n- Iftikhar Ali Khan Pataudi died on 5 January 1952.\n- From 1952, Mansoor Ali Khan Pataudi was the titular Nawab of Pataudi.\n- Mansoor Ali Khan Pataudi, known as the Nawab of Pataudi Jr., later served as captain of the India cricket team.\n- In 1971, the 26th Amendment to the Constitution of India abolished the privy purses of the princes and ended official recognition of their titles, ending Mansoor Ali Khan Pataudi’s titular status as Nawab of Pataudi.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
