        "text": "Page: Iftikhar Ali Khan Pataudi. Sentence: Iftikhar Ali Khan, sometimes I. A. K. Pataudi (16 March 1910 – 5 January 1952) was the 8th Nawab of Pataudi and the captain of the India national cricket team for the tour to England in 1946.\nPage: Iftikhar Ali Khan Pataudi. Sentence: His son Mansoor, known as the Nawab of Pataudi Jr., also later served as captain of the India cricket team.\nPage: Mansoor Ali Khan Pataudi. Sentence: He was the titular Nawab of Pataudi from 1952 until 1971, when by the 26th Amendment to the Constitution of India the privy purses of the princes were abolished and official recognition of their titles came to an end.",
